WEBVTT

1
00:00:07.383 --> 00:00:09.224
The lion was very strong.

2
00:00:09.904 --> 00:00:12.605
He was the king of all the other animals.

3
00:00:14.126 --> 00:00:16.366
One day the lion met a monkey.

4
00:00:16.386 --> 00:00:19.108
"Good morning, Your Majesty!

5
00:00:19.128 --> 00:00:22.969
Your mane looks wonderful today," said the monkey.

6
00:00:22.989 --> 00:00:24.950
"Of course!"

7
00:00:25.510 --> 00:00:26.531
agreed the lion.

8
00:00:27.371 --> 00:00:32.105
Suddenly the monkey held his nose, "Oh my!"

9
00:00:32.125 --> 00:00:36.647
"Is something wrong, little monkey?"

10
00:00:37.167 --> 00:00:38.048
asked the lion.

11
00:00:38.068 --> 00:00:40.469
"Uh, no, no.

12
00:00:41.110 --> 00:00:41.810
Nothing, sir."

13
00:00:41.830 --> 00:00:44.792
"Then why did you make such a face?

14
00:00:45.612 --> 00:00:46.653
Tell me the truth!"

15
00:00:47.273 --> 00:00:48.554
the lion commanded.

16
00:00:48.574 --> 00:00:52.376
"Well, uh," the monkey trembled.

17
00:00:52.396 --> 00:00:54.897
"Your breath smells bad.

18
00:00:55.357 --> 00:00:55.897
That's all."

19
00:00:55.917 --> 00:01:00.280
"My breath smells bad?

20
00:01:00.824 --> 00:01:01.725
Is that all?"

21
00:01:02.285 --> 00:01:03.446
repeated the lion.

22
00:01:03.466 --> 00:01:04.948
"Oh yes!

23
00:01:05.628 --> 00:01:06.609
Yes, that's it.

24
00:01:07.169 --> 00:01:07.790
That's all!"

25
00:01:08.290 --> 00:01:09.111
said the monkey.

26
00:01:09.131 --> 00:01:13.414
"Okay, then you will never smell it again!"

27
00:01:14.335 --> 00:01:16.677
And the lion ate the monkey up.

28
00:01:18.258 --> 00:01:20.260
The lion was still angry.

29
00:01:20.981 --> 00:01:23.362
So he stopped a rabbit passing by.

30
00:01:23.382 --> 00:01:24.864
"You there!

31
00:01:25.304 --> 00:01:29.908
Stop! Come here and smell my breath," he ordered.

32
00:01:30.744 --> 00:01:33.526
"Me? Oh yes, my king."

33
00:01:34.166 --> 00:01:35.667
The rabbit was scared.

34
00:01:36.408 --> 00:01:41.051
When the lion breathed, she groaned, "Ohh!"

35
00:01:42.211 --> 00:01:45.433
"Does it smell good or bad?"

36
00:01:46.034 --> 00:01:47.155
the lion asked.

37
00:01:49.256 --> 00:01:52.118
The rabbit knew that the lion ate the monkey.

38
00:01:53.018 --> 00:01:55.360
So she lied to the lion.

39
00:01:56.653 --> 00:02:01.356
"Oh, my king, your breath smells wonderful."

40
00:02:01.376 --> 00:02:05.059
"Is that so?

41
00:02:05.719 --> 00:02:08.041
How wonderful does it smell?"

42
00:02:08.681 --> 00:02:09.382
he asked.

43
00:02:09.402 --> 00:02:18.508
"Umm, uh, your breath smells fruity like an apple," said the rabbit.

44
00:02:18.528 --> 00:02:21.250
"You are lying to me!"

45
00:02:21.270 --> 00:02:22.471
growled the lion.

46
00:02:24.028 --> 00:02:26.610
So he ate the rabbit up too.

47
00:02:28.592 --> 00:02:31.634
The fox saw all of this from behind a tree.

48
00:02:32.375 --> 00:02:36.058
He was so terrified that he tried to run away.

49
00:02:36.078 --> 00:02:39.981
"You, little fox," called the lion.

50
00:02:40.001 --> 00:02:41.302
"Stop there!"

51
00:02:41.322 --> 00:02:45.946
"Ah oh, yes, my king!"

52
00:02:46.526 --> 00:02:47.507
answered the fox.

53
00:02:47.527 --> 00:02:53.072
"Come here and smell my breath," said the lion.

54
00:02:54.800 --> 00:03:00.042
The poor little fox had no choice but to smell the lion's breath.

55
00:03:00.742 --> 00:03:02.502
The lion breathed.

56
00:03:02.982 --> 00:03:03.863
"How was it?

57
00:03:04.423 --> 00:03:06.603
Was it good or bad?"

58
00:03:06.623 --> 00:03:09.684
"Umm what should I tell him?"

59
00:03:10.184 --> 00:03:11.205
thought the fox.

60
00:03:12.785 --> 00:03:15.526
The lion's breath smelled really bad.

61
00:03:16.286 --> 00:03:18.367
The fox could not lie to him.

62
00:03:19.107 --> 00:03:23.268
But he could not tell the lion what it was really like either.

63
00:03:24.264 --> 00:03:26.186
"Why don't you say something?"

64
00:03:26.706 --> 00:03:27.767
the lion asked.

65
00:03:27.787 --> 00:03:31.570
"Do you think my breath smells bad?"

66
00:03:31.590 --> 00:03:40.036
"Oh, no, my king, I, I, uh," said the fox, thinking quickly.

67
00:03:40.056 --> 00:03:41.897
"I have a cold.

68
00:03:42.578 --> 00:03:44.399
Yes, I have a cold!

69
00:03:45.160 --> 00:03:47.061
So my nose is very stuffy.

70
00:03:47.782 --> 00:03:50.804
I cannot smell anything very well," he said.

71
00:03:50.824 --> 00:03:54.075
"I can only guess that your breath smells good.

72
00:03:54.996 --> 00:03:55.937
What do you think?"

73
00:03:56.417 --> 00:03:57.098
he asked.

74
00:03:57.118 --> 00:04:01.082
"Ahh, hmm.

75
00:04:02.123 --> 00:04:06.668
Yes, I am sure it smells good," said the lion.

76
00:04:06.688 --> 00:04:09.971
"Sure!" agreed the fox.

77
00:04:10.832 --> 00:04:14.196
And the satisfied lion let the fox live.
